bed nodule  with closest  anterior  margin  C  remainder of well circumscribed nodule  with posterior margin  D E  mass with closest  posterior  margin F  mass  G I  biopsy cavity with closest  anterior  margin  J  representative sections away from masses  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional right axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of tan pink fibroadipose tissue  A 1 2cm lymph node is identified which is bisected and submitted entirely in K  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in L  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is examined for lymph nodes  which are submitted as follows  M N  one 2 4cm firm lymph node  serially sectioned and entirely submitted  O P  one 2 5cm lymph node  bisected  Q  one potential 0 6cm lymph node  bisected  R T  multiple potential lymph nodes  0 3cm to 1 3cm in greatest dimension  submitted whole  U  one 1 5cm lymph node  bisected  V  multiple potential lymph nodes  0 4cm to 0 7cm in greatest dimension  submitted whole  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shaved margins  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue that is unoriented  The specimen is entirely submitted in W CC  Resident  ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  REMOVED_DATE CM CIRCUMSCRIBED NODULE ADJACENT TO A REMOVED_DATE CM FIRM SUSPICIOUS AREA REMOVED_DATE CM TO THE CLOSEST MARGIN  POSTERIOR   REMOVED_DATE CM BIOPSY CAVITY  REMOVED_DATE CM TO THE CLOSEST MARGIN  ANTERIOR   O R  Resident  ELENA BRACHTEL  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT 