Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 45 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO ABOUT 1MM OF AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  CONFINED TO THE MASS AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO ABOUT 1MM OF AN INKED MARGIN  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA   LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  PRESENT IN 3 OF 8 SLIDES  APPROXIMATELY REMOVED_DATE CM TOTAL   FOCALLY EXTENDING TO AN INKED MARGIN  CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE   LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 16 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone recpetor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast mass   are two fragments of breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm respectively  inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined tan white firm nodule about REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm extending to 0 4cm from the nearest margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and resubmitted in A  The remaining nodule is submitted entirely in cassettes B D  The rest of the parenchyma of the large fragment and the smaller fragment are unremarkable  A representative section of the larger fragment is in E  and representative sections of the smaller fragment are in F  Received n formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  re excision of mass   are two fragments of fatty soft tissue  The larger fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and has an ellipse of skin attached measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  A hemorrhagic polypoid mass is attached to this fragment and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The smaller fragment of tissue measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm with a