e F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen which consists of a left breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with an inverted T shaped overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm axillary tail  The skin surface is studded with multiple REMOVED_DATE to 0 6cm skin colored papules diffusely across its surface  The nipple is unremarkable and no definitive old scars are identified  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm tan white stellate infiltrating nodule is identified corresponding to the 2 o clock region of the specimen  It comes to 0 5cm from the closest  anterior  margin and 1 2cm from the posterior margin  As well  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm tan white stellate infiltrating nodule is present corresponding to the 10 o clock region of the specimen and it is 1 5cm from the closest  posterior  margin  Multiple smaller  similar in appearance nodules are present throughout the breast parenchyma ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 1cm in greatest dimension  The closest of which approaches the posterior margin to 0 8cm  They are present primarily in the mid portion of the specimen  Axillary lymph nodes as large as 1 6cm in greatest dimension are identified  The cut surface is firm and tan pink  Section code  G   2 o clock mass and sections of posterior margin adjacent to mass  H   2 o clock mass and adjacent anterior margin I  representative section of 10 o clock lesion and representative section of 10 o clock region with adjacent closest posterior margin  J   representative section of 10 o clock lesion with adjacent anterior margin K M  representative sections of other parenchymal nodules and representative section of skin papule  N R  axillary lymph nodes completely submitted S   axillary lymph node bivalved  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  are multiple fragm