x 1 8cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fatty parenchyma  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A through J  Labeled  left breast  is a 27 x 23 x 6cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 10 x 9 x 4cm attached axillary tail and a suture marking the highest axillary node  The surface of the specimen has a REMOVED_DATE x 5cm irregular  skin ellipse with a nipple as well as a 3 5cm curvilinear  well healed scar  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm hemorrhagic  multiloculated cyst with surrounding fibrosis  0 1cm from the deep resection margin  7cm from the inferior margin  3 8cm from the anterior margin  8cm from the medial margin  7cm from the lateral margin  and 8cm from the superior margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 3cm area of firm  tan white tissue with fat necrosis and a gritty cut surface superficial to the cyst  2cm from the anterior margin  6 8cm from the inferior margin  and 3cm from the deep margin  The cyst is surrounded by fibrous tissue and the remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted as follows  K L  Cyst wall with deep resection margin  M  Representative sections of cyst wall  N  Representative section of firm  gritty area  anterior to the cyst wall  O  Representative section of firm  gritty area and cyst wall  P  Representative section of firm breast parenchyma adjacent to cyst wall  Q  Representative section of nipple and skin ellipse  Numerous lymph nodes are dissected away from the axillary fat and submitted as follows  R  Highest axillary lymph node  three   Representative sections of the lymph nodes from the remainder of the axillary dissection are submitted in cassettes S through Z  Labeled  left axillary nodes  are several fragments of fibroadipose tissue  3 x 2 x 1cm in aggregate  No lymph nodes are identified  Tissue is submitted entirely in cassette AA  Labeled  left breast fla