tions with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 00     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Three specimens are received fresh  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Designated  right breast and axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen oriented by a short stitch superior and a long stitch lateral  with an overlying triangular  REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple areola complex  There are no scars in the overlying skin  However  there is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm erythematous area  with a palpable firmness 5 0cm inferior to the nipple  The excised surface is inked black  Cross sectioning reveals an ill defined firm  white REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nodule  located 2 0cm beneath the inferior portion of the skin  and coming to within 2 2cm of the nearest margin  deep   There is firm white fibrous tissue extending away from the nodule and a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of hemorrhage extending from this white fibrous tissue anterior to the overlying skin suggestive of a prior biopsy site  These changes are located beneath the erythematous nodule visible on the skin surface  Approximately 1 0cm anterior and medial to this lesion is a second very firm yellow tan  well demarcated nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which comes to within 1 8cm 