 healed  horizontal scar superior to the nipple  The scar is focally at the superior  12 o clock skin edge  In addition  the skin surface has multiple raised velvety tan to light brown plaques  which range from REMOVED_DATE to 1 8cm in greatest dimension  Cross section reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  firm  tan brown  hemorrhagic mass with a gritty cut surface  The central portion of the tumor is hemorrhagic  and a metal clip  which measures 0 3cm in length x 0 1cm in thickness  is extracted from the center of the lesion  The mass is located 2cm from the closest posterior margin  2 7cm from the closest anterior margin  and 2 5cm from the closest skin surface  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm round nodule in the lower outer quadrant  This nodule is 0 4cm from the mass and appears unrelated to it  The small nodule is 2cm from the closest anterior margin  2cm from the closest skin surface  and 4 5cm from the closest posterior margin  The scar in the mid superior portion of the breast does not have an underlying biopsy cavity  this area is a grossly unremarkable fatty breast parenchyma  No lymph nodes are seen in the axillary portion of the specimen  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of the closest anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Separate small nodule submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section away from the cavity including skin with well healed scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the axillary tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the velvety skin lesion  Note  Please note the mass is located 5cm away from the skin scar  Gross Dictation by Julia Turbiner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Julia Turbiner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMP