ral biopsy cavity V W   anterior biopsy cavity H   medial and posterior biopsy cavity I   inferior and posterior biopsy cavity J K L Y Z AA BB   all sections lateral to the biopsy cavity Examination of the axillary contents measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm reveals ten lymph nodes which range in dimension from 0 4cm to 3 0cm  The largest lymph node has focal areas of hemorrhage and fat replacement  Sections of axillary fat and representative lymph nodes are submitted in M   T  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
