eceptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 95 at 15 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm breast and axillary tail with an overlying ellipse of skin  REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  There is a 4 0cm line about 3 5cm from the nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm cavity is present about 1 0cm from the deep inked margin and 1 5cm from the overlying skin  The wall of the cavity is hard  tan and nodular in several areas  but otherwise smooth  The breast parenchyma around the biopsy cavity is rubbery  tan and slightly nodular  The rest of breast parenchyma is unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A  closest margin to biopsy cavity on the deep inked margin  B E  representative sections of wall of the biopsy cavity  F H  representative sections of fibrous area around the biopsy cavity  I L  lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  a