Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 22 CLINICAL DATA  Palpable nodule                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   RIGHT BREAST MASS    BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3   PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  WITH FOCI HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE  HIGH GRADE   ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT AND FOCALLY LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED SURFACE  NOTE  Definite vascular invasion is not seen  The intra operative gross diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 13     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PROTEIN AS REPORTED BY IMPATH 1 800 447  REMOVED_CASE_ID  BREAST  RIGHT   30  OF THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PROTEIN  THE RESULT FALLS IN THE UNFAVORABLE CATEGORY  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of breast which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  white to yellow nodule abutting the inked margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through E  with the nodule in A through C  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  SINGLE FIRM WHITE NODULE REMOVED_DATE CM IN DIAMETER  SUSPICIOUS BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
