ty to overlying skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional cavity to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of uninvolved parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of uninvolved parenchyma to fibrotic  Received in formalin  and labeled  right breast additional tissue   are 4 fragments of skin covered soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The largest fragment is notable for a nodular surface of the overlying skin  The specimen are all serially sectioned to reveal a homogenous white tan firm cut surface with no obvious mass  hemorrhage or calcifications  Representative sections from each of the 4 fragments in ascending order of size are submitted from  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 55 23PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Breast  Right Additional   Excision  report_end  , Checked.
