ce or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 07 Proofread by  SELIM NASSER  MD GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast and axillary sampling   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fatty tissue  designated as axillary sampling  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior black  anterior blue  superior orange  inferior green  The specimen is sectioned two separate hard spiculated irregular nodules in the central region of the breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm and REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm repectively  These nodules are more than 0 7cm from the closets margin which is the depp margin  The remainder of the breast tissue is firm  representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Inferior margin B  Superior margin C  Medial margin D  Lateral margin E  Smaller nodule with deep margin F  Deep margino G  Anterior margin H N  representative sections from firm breast tissue  O  2 nodes P  2 nodes Q  1 node II  3 nodes CC FF HH  Larger nodule DD EE  Fibroadenoma Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional latera left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of fatty breast tissue  The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal no focal lesions  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes R BB  Resident  LYNN CORNELL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Jonathan Michael Winograd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT LATERAL TISSUE   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 40 CLINICAL DATA  75 y o  female undergoing excisional biopsy of a left breast mass detected by mammography  Core   adenocarcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITH EXTENSIVE MUCIN PRODUCTION  CELLULAR MUCINOUS CARCINOMA   GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   LATERAL MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of breast tissue with a stitch marking the anterior lateral margin as denoted by the surgeon  The specimen is inked black and the anterior lateral half has been overinked green  It is sectioned to reveal a a firm area 0 3cm in greatest dimension  The firm area is submitted in A  with the remainder submitted in B through I  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  lateral margin tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of breast tissue that is inked and submitted in its entirety in cassette J  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  SMALL FIRM AREA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENT  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 53 CLINICAL DATA  63 year old female with biopsy proven right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3  90   REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10   SINGLE FOCUS  COMEDO TYPE  3  BREAST ATROPHY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Inked resection margins are free of carcinoma  the closest margin is at least 0 5cm  from tumor  There is no evidence of lymphatic or vascular invasion  Carcinoma is present in two of fifteen slides  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 15 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fibroadipose tissue with wire in place and x ray demonstrating an ill defined stellate lesion  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 5cm firm gritty region with a central hemorrhagic cavity  This area is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted in cassette A  Remaining tissue from that region is submitted in cassette B  Additional representative sections of tissue are submitted in cassettes C through O  Labeled  Axillary contents  is a piece of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  Several lymph nodes are identified within this tissue  The largest lymph node is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The largest two are bisected and submitted entirely in cassettes P and Q  respectively  Remaining lymph nodes in R through T  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH