ith this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 97 at 15 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are three separate specimens   Left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of breast tissue with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin ellipse containing an ill defined scar  Specimen is inked as follows  lateral black  superior red  inferior green  medial yellow  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm well circumscribed  tan to pink mass is present which is approximately 0 2cm from the inferior  green  and approximately 0 4cm from the superior  red  resection margins  No frozen section is done  The specimen with closest inferior margin in A  closest superior margin in B  closest lateral margin in C  and closest medial margin in D  An additional representative section of tumor is submitted in E  The surrounding breast parenchyma is scant  and contains areas of focal fibrosis  representative section of surrounding tissue and skin ellipse in F   Left breast mass new superior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with the superior margin inked blue  lateral margin inked green  medial margin inked yellow  and inferior margin inked black  Specimen is entirely submitted in G th